            <div xml:id="d510">

                <pb facs="0467" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/640.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexican Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-01-11"><hi rendition="#italic">January 11,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 620.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    receipt of your excellency’s note number 377 of the 5th instant with which you
                    were pleased to transmit to me the communication of the United States attorney
                    for the western district of Texas, relative to the vigilance exercised by the
                    American authorities along the boundary line to prevent any violation of the
                    neutrality laws.</p>
                <p>The embassy appreciates to their full value the efforts of the said authorities
                    and hopes, in view of the sentiments which animate the Government of the United
                    States, that they will prevent and energetically repress all punishable acts
                    committed in violation of the statutes.</p>
                <p>I renew [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. L. de la
                    Barra.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
